From: Linexa Engineering <linexa@fem.linexa>
Date: 2026-08-25
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] ashmem_memfd: include <string.h> for strcmp/memset

Required to compile termux/proot v5.1.107.89 with modern clang (NDK r29):
implicit function declarations are errors under C99+, and ashmem_memfd.c
calls strcmp(3) and memset(3) without including <string.h>.

Cosmetic build fix only — no behavior change.

diff --git a/src/extension/ashmem_memfd/ashmem_memfd.c b/src/extension/ashmem_memfd/ashmem_memfd.c
--- a/src/extension/ashmem_memfd/ashmem_memfd.c
+++ b/src/extension/ashmem_memfd/ashmem_memfd.c
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 #if defined(__ANDROID__) || defined(__BIONIC__)

 #include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
 #include <signal.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
 #include <sys/syscall.h>  /* __NR_memfd_create,  */
